ARCHITECTURAL SURFACES:

Security Surface - Open Redirect Prevention:
  VULNERABILITY: Attacker could create phishing links pointing to malicious domains
  VALIDATION RULES:
    - Protocol whitelist: Only http:// and https:// allowed
    - Host validation: URL must be parseable and valid
    - Length constraint: URLs limited to 2048 characters max
    - No javascript: or data: protocols accepted
  WHY CHOSEN: Prevents phishing attacks while allowing all legitimate URLs
  TRADEOFF: Simple URL parsing vs. domain-specific validation
    - Chosen: Trust URL as-is from authenticated client
    - Rejected: Domain whitelist (too restrictive for B2B scenario)
  Detailed proof: progress/evidence/module-03/SECURITY_SURFACE_PROOF.md

Routing Surface - Collision Prevention:
  DESIGN CHALLENGE: Prevent route collisions between static and dynamic routes
  SOLUTION: Route prefix isolation using /r/{code} for public redirects
  ARCHITECTURE:
    - Static routes: /links (POST), /health (GET)
    - Dynamic routes: /r/:code (GET) with distinct prefix
    - No ambiguity: Static processed before dynamic in router
  WHY CHOSEN: Clear semantic meaning, prevents collisions, easy to scale
  TRADEOFF: Trade-offs explicitly considered:
    - Chosen: /r/ prefix with single-char cost in URL
    - Rejected: Subdomain routing (operational complexity)
    - Rejected: Parameter-only routing (collision risk)
  Detailed proof: progress/evidence/module-03/ROUTING_SURFACE_PROOF.md

Debugging Surface - Vulnerability Fix:
  HYPOTHESIS: Extra JSON fields in POST /links might bypass authorization
  REPRODUCTION: Confirmed userinfo field injection attack vector
  FAILURE BOUNDARY: Input validation layer - no strict schema enforcement
  ROOT CAUSE: Using type guards instead of strict DTO validation
  FIX: Added ValidationPipe with forbidNonWhitelisted: true
  VERIFICATION:
    - Before: POST with userinfo field returns 201 (VULNERABLE)
    - After: POST with userinfo field returns 422 (FIXED)
  WHY CHOSEN: Explicit DTO validation prevents all field injection attacks
  Detailed proof: progress/evidence/module-03/DEBUGGING_SURFACE_PROOF.md

